{"id": "EUVD-2026-80624", "enisaUuid": "5b1f7f0e-fbc2-3c6f-9f77-d73dcf02c882", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nstaging: rtl8723bs: fix OOB read in rtw_restruct_wmm_ie()\n\nrtw_restruct_wmm_ie() scans in_ie for a WMM IE with:\n\n\twhile (i < in_len) {\n\t\t...\n\t\tif (i + 5 < in_len && in_ie[i] == 0xDD && ...) {\n\t\t\t...\n\t\t\tbreak;\n\t\t}\n\t\ti += (in_ie[i + 1] + 2); /* to the next IE element */\n\t}\n\nWhen the \"i + 5 < in_len\" match check fails simply because i is\nwithin 5 bytes of the end of the buffer (i.e. no WMM IE was found\nnear the tail of in_ie), execution falls through to\n\"i += (in_ie[i + 1] + 2)\", which reads in_ie[i + 1]. If i == in_len\n- 1 at that point, this is a 1-byte out-of-bounds read of an\nattacker-influenced IE buffer built from association/scan data.\n\nCommit a75281626fc8f (\"staging: rtl8723bs: fix potential\nout-of-bounds read in rtw_restruct_wmm_ie\") added the \"i + 5 <\nin_len\" guard to the match condition itself, but did not add an\nequivalent guard before the fallthrough advance, so the same class\nof OOB read remained reachable through the non-matching path.\n\nAdd an explicit bounds check before advancing to the next IE.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:33:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:49:26", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/716850842d2f103f915fe7c857ff1a0a036491b4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e63b72c5d7336981dfc05e5cb92becff29dfea00", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4420cc71841b50e31a7868ef7acb011c0e08d294", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fd19b8895f8a91087e8a62f1e27b128025dabb95", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/28a289beaf226b30b1e6e7d7b1a2946fe2d6e852"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90016", "GHSA-54jr-3vx9-2c5p"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "023bb469-0f83-3ca8-87e5-b1d3202d8eb5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "03131ba4-6c96-353b-b139-dce6a4bfccad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "0f9782ce-9ba1-3352-b872-51f95df7ae7d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "554c0a3abf216c991c5ebddcdb2c08689ecd290b <e63b72c5d7336981dfc05e5cb92becff29dfea00"}, {"id": "352573c4-2d4b-3dc8-aca4-69372701cbec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.12"}, {"id": "55921e2d-9a23-3ce5-bffc-c26dcee28bb0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "554c0a3abf216c991c5ebddcdb2c08689ecd290b <fd19b8895f8a91087e8a62f1e27b128025dabb95"}, {"id": "651e277e-a7aa-3adb-a9ae-55b751c05bd3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "6711137b-04ef-3319-9e12-e5f554d1577a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "554c0a3abf216c991c5ebddcdb2c08689ecd290b <28a289beaf226b30b1e6e7d7b1a2946fe2d6e852"}, {"id": "6adec4e9-7158-35a5-a5ae-5f66c8c8e617", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "957cd611-5fb8-3ca6-93f7-3d1a4f1fce51", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "c6cf41bd-3708-3dcd-a1fd-8a309508ef93", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "554c0a3abf216c991c5ebddcdb2c08689ecd290b <4420cc71841b50e31a7868ef7acb011c0e08d294"}, {"id": "db474800-ce56-3041-a806-73a84dc4bba8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "554c0a3abf216c991c5ebddcdb2c08689ecd290b <716850842d2f103f915fe7c857ff1a0a036491b4"}, {"id": "de753d37-2784-36c7-a6e9-96a58afe0f97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor"